{
  "findings": [
    {
      "ref": "[D536]",
      "area": "contact",
      "claim": "A parent reports that strangers can send messages and friend requests to a child, and these cannot be disabled.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "other users can send messages and friend requests although these are audited for language as appropriate to the age of the player is important to ensure that unwanted interactions with strangers are not occurring along with the usual advice to play games together with younger players and keep them in shared family spaces there are some good parenting controls on roblox that ensure your child has an appropriate experience the first thing to ensure is that you entered their age correctly so that the appropriate safe chat mode is applied to their accounts their age however does not feel to the types of games they can play on roblox to restrict the list of games to a safe list curated by roblox go in to your account on the robots website click the gear icon select settings security and then enable account restrictions you can also restrict the online interactions with different players by the roblox website again click the gear icon on the top right select settings privacy then restrict the interactions via content settings and other settings associating your email address to the account will notify you when friend requests come in there is no way to disable these friend requests and you need to click ignore in the game to do away with them"
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D536]",
      "area": "money",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Roblox incentivizes children to spend money on in-app purchases to buy gear and vehicles.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "finally although roblox is free-to-play there are in-app purchases in the game to buy extra gear and extra vehicles or advance more quickly children are incentivized to pay for these and to ask for more roblox money so it is important that you set up the appropriate passwords on any credit cards associated with your account"
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D536]",
      "area": "data",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Roblox collects personal data and shares it with third parties for advertising, and that data can be deleted.",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "quote": "the video standards council expanded on the pegi rating by saying, \"Violence is very mild and consists of blocky, action-figure and stick-like humanoid characters competing in various child-friendly games. Armed with fists, swords or guns they can hit each other until they fall apart and disappear. Blood and injuries are not depicted.\" They specifically looked at sample games (made by the developer themselves rather than users) at the time of rating, \"Violence can be found in the following games: Coalesce, Fisticuffs, Heroes, Ripull Minigames, ROBLOX Dodgeball, Skybound II, Super Check Point and TNT Rush.\""
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D536]",
