      "claim": "A parent reports that some user-generated games contain horror, violence, and blood, such as Hotline Roblox where players attack each other with knives and guns and see pixelated blood.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "One example is the Hotline Roblox game where players attack each other with knives and guns until they fall over and then attack the prone bodies to kill them whereupon picks a weighted blood splatters are seen being an online game parents should also pay attention to interactions with their children other users can send messages and friend requests although these are audited for language as appropriate to the age of the player is important to ensure that unwanted interactions with strangers are not occurring along with the usual advice to play games together with younger players and keep them in shared family spaces there are some good parenting controls on roblox that ensure your child has an appropriate experience the first thing to ensure is that you entered their age correctly so that the appropriate safe chat mode is applied to their accounts their age however does not feel to the types of games they can play on roblox to restrict the list of games to a safe list curated by roblox go in to your account on the robots website click the gear icon select settings security and then enable account restrictions you can also restrict the online interactions with different players by the roblox website again click the gear icon on the top right select settings privacy then restrict the interactions via content settings and other settings associating your email address to the account will notify you when friend requests come in there is no way to disable these friend requests and you need to click ignore in the game to do away with them"
